# Cloudflare Tunnel ingress rules for the SAP DM MQTT stack
#
# This stack does NOT run its own cloudflared container.
# Add the rules below to your EXISTING Cloudflare Tunnel config
# (the one already serving jellyfin.haegens.be and other services).
#
# Find your tunnel config at the path shown by:
#   cloudflared tunnel info <your-tunnel-name>
# Typically: ~/.cloudflared/config.yml  or  /etc/cloudflared/config.yml
#
# Paste these three ingress rules into the existing ingress: list.
# Rule ordering matters: Cloudflare evaluates rules top-to-bottom and stops
# at the first match. The HTTP path rules (/editor, /dashboard) must come
# BEFORE the WebSocket catch-all (no path field), otherwise all traffic for
# this hostname goes to Mosquitto and the dashboard/editor are unreachable.
#
# Replace 192.168.x.x with the LAN IP of the sapdm-demo LXC.

# --- paste into your existing ingress: list ---
#
#   - hostname: mqttfordm.haegens.be
#     path: /editor.*
#     service: http://192.168.x.x:80
#
#   - hostname: mqttfordm.haegens.be
#     path: /dashboard.*
#     service: http://192.168.x.x:80
#
#   - hostname: mqttfordm.haegens.be
#     service: ws://192.168.x.x:9001
#
# --- end of rules to paste ---
#
# After editing, reload your tunnel:
#   cloudflared tunnel reload
# or restart the cloudflared service:
#   systemctl restart cloudflared
